 ## T031 proposed coordinated publication boundary
 
 Source-only investigation at `c2babf6a0195a88d1cf895e22fffa8d561e847e3`, 2026-10-01; those production bytes are unchanged in accepted T030-E normal source `29f485748819a8d95fd94b483f96e98c3f6e4b81`. The proposal below preserves the complete read-only report's useful caller/contract/verification findings. **T031 is not implemented or verified by this record.** It completes neither full accepted-turn acceptance nor browser/worker/save-load migration. Source locations are relative to the repository at the inspected source.
@@ -292,6 +294,8 @@ Prefer migrating **helper-specific** fault injections to the existing synchronou
 
 Do not replay old callbacks after commit, ignore returned Tasks, or block arbitrary async callbacks with sync-over-async. Preserving the arbitrary internal `Func<PlannedWrite,Task>` contract would require a genuinely awaited observer path through B1 and is a wider alternative. There is no observed production need for that alternative. Collapsing duplicates necessarily changes synthetic intermediate-image hook observations; state the revised test contract as one observation per published unique final member.
 
+Chosen T031-A refinement (2026-10-01): retain the original-recorder browser acceptance callback on its existing route. Ordinary helper storage cuts move to B1; invalid mixed ordinary-publication/legacy-callback use must fail explicitly. The actual ordinary acceptance and next-wave tests must assert both the reached pre-decision member cut and absence of service acknowledgment. The existing `final:mechanics/history/runtime`, transport deletion and `final:continuation` controls remain later gameplay compensation tests, including exact restoration and retry identity reuse. `QteSceneServiceTests.ResolveActiveActionAsync_BackupCleanupFailureDoesNotMaskCommittedResult` remains a post-acceptance cleanup control. A test-only hook name does not make these boundaries semantically interchangeable. At the time this refinement was recorded, the first four-test helper scaffold had not run; the current plan records later execution and the still-pending consumer refinements.
